    "created_at": "2016-10-07T17:43:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-07T17:43:04Z",
    "body": "This area was previously discussed in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1358. Basically the issue is a lot more complex and ideally we'd be figuring out what browsers actually do and speccing that. But we should definitely consider short-term fixes if they'd clarify the situation for implementers.\n\nCould you clarify when a pointerup would be fired but a click/mouseup/another event from that list would not? That would give us some indication of how to test this (even manually).\n\nIf this change ends up being desired as-is, regarding the reference issues, you'll need to fix things by adding a reference to the pointer events spec (as the CI failure is telling you). You can copy the pattern already used for UI events and touch events. (\"The following features are defined in the Touch Events specification\".) At some point we'll probably want to add pointer and touch events to the list of global event handlers, but that's a separate topic.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/252315630/reactions",
